WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.191 --> 00:00:08.389
A replay of 6 real Kensa runs, recorded with a local model (qwen3:4b) on a 4 GB laptop GPU. Nothing is running now.

2
00:00:08.391 --> 00:00:12.855
A built-in sample: "Frontend build fails an environment check".

3
00:00:12.857 --> 00:00:26.368
Every claim cites a source line. The verifier found 4 of 4 quotes on their cited lines (1 in the job log, 3 in knowledge-base notes), and the log itself states the cause: "Cause corroborated".

4
00:00:26.369 --> 00:00:33.397
A citation of the log opens its line in the stored log; other citations open their evidence excerpt.

5
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:37.660
Fixes are proposals only. Kensa never changes a repository.

6
00:00:37.662 --> 00:00:43.255
In the replay, a decision is kept in this browser tab only. Nothing is saved.

7
00:00:43.257 --> 00:00:49.450
A failing test is a symptom, so a test regression is at most "Plausible, not confirmed".

8
00:00:49.452 --> 00:01:01.823
The model's proposals are shown as produced, mistakes included: 2 of the 5 would change the test instead of the code. Each carries the risk that this hides a real regression.

9
00:01:01.825 --> 00:01:08.664
This log does not show the failure, so Kensa does not ask the model to guess: "Not established".

10
00:01:08.666 --> 00:01:15.361
The interface is also in Japanese. Recorded model output stays in English.
